@startuml package_overview
title HydroModPy — Diagramme de packages (dependances reelles, verifiees par grep import)
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "core" as core #F5F5F5
package "config" as config #F5F5F5
package "physics" as physics #E8F0FE
package "spatial" as spatial #E8F0FE
package "data" as data #E8F0FE
package "solver" as solver #FCE8E6
package "simulation" as simulation #FCE8E6
package "workflow" as workflow #FCE8E6
package "results" as results #E6F4EA
package "calibration" as calibration #FEF7E0
package "project" as project #FEF7E0
package "analysis" as analysis #FEF7E0
package "display" as display #E6F4EA
package "reporting" as reporting #E6F4EA
package "cli" as cli #FFFFFF
package "discretization" as discretization #F5F5F5
package "schema" as schema #F5F5F5
package "catalog" as catalog #F5F5F5

' -- Couche 0 : infrastructure, aucune dependance montante
' core n'importe ni config/, ni data/, ni spatial/, ni physics/
config --> core
schema --> config
discretization --> core

' -- Couche 1 : modeles scientifiques / geometrie, solveur-agnostiques
physics --> core
spatial --> core
data --> core
data ..> spatial : GeologyDataSource (Protocol)

' -- Couche 2 : solveurs numeriques (importent physics, jamais l'inverse)
solver --> physics
solver --> spatial
solver --> core
note on link
  confirme par grep :
  solver/ importe physics/ (25 fichiers)
  physics/ n'importe JAMAIS solver/ (0 fichier)
end note

' -- Couche 3 : execution
simulation --> core
simulation ..> solver : SolverRegistryProvider (Protocol,\nresolution paresseuse via registry)
workflow --> core
workflow --> data
workflow --> spatial
workflow ..> simulation : Launcher (Protocol, SimulationRunner)
workflow ..> results : SimulationCatalog (ouvert par les Steps)

' -- Couche 4 : resultats et catalogue
results --> core
results --> spatial : Grid/Mesh (types)

' -- Couche 5 : facade et orchestrateurs haut niveau
project --> workflow
project --> results
project --> data
project --> spatial
project --> config
calibration --> core
calibration ..> workflow : TrialPipelineProvider (Protocol,\ninversion de dependance)
calibration ..> project : TrialPromotionProvider (Protocol,\nimplemente par project.dispatch)
calibration ..> solver : CalibrationSeriesExtractor (Protocol)

' -- Couche 6 : presentation
display --> results
display ..> workflow : DisplayStep ouvre SimulationCatalog
reporting --> results
reporting --> calibration
reporting ..> display : figures (via _SessionRunStub)
analysis --> core
analysis ..> project : TestbedRunnerProvider (Protocol,\nimplemente par project.dispatch)
analysis ..> workflow

catalog --> data

' -- Entree utilisateur
cli ..> project : hmp.run() / hmp.calibrate() (API fonctionnelle _api.py)
cli --> workflow : workflow.dispatch.resolve_workflow()
cli --> project : project.dispatch.workflow.dispatch_workflow()

note as NLegend
  **Legende**
  --> dependance directe (import)
  ..> dependance inversee via Protocol
      (Ports & Adapters -- le package "bas" definit
      le Protocol, un package "haut" fournit l'implementation
      enregistree a l'exécution)

  **Regle d'architecture centrale** (core/state/run_state.py) :
  core/ ne peut importer ni config/, ni data/, ni spatial/,
  ni physics/ -- communication uniquement via core.contracts.*
  (Protocol) ou champs typés Any (WorkflowContext.cfg).
end note

note as NEmpty
  Packages vides (code legacy, seuls des .pyc fantomes
  subsistent) : process/, mesh/, grid/, geographic/,
  watershed/, metamodel/, field/, data_managers/, pyhelp/,
  calibration_legacy/. Non representes.
end note

@enduml
